1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,480
“I can’t tell my family what I want without feeling ungrateful.”
Fictional · prepared scenario.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:06,950
For adults facing family pressure: clarify privately,
correct the reflection, choose whether to share.

3
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:13,900
Arjun puts the family pressure into his own words.

4
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:20,850
Muse Spark is planned to help organize themes for review.
This text is prepared; no model is connected.

5
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:27,050
Prepared local example · no model connected.
A possible reading for Arjun to check.

6
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:32,100
“Not quite.” The first reading misses what he needs.

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:39,100
He says he needs time to decide for himself.

8
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:44,950
The editable reflection changes to hold his correction.

9
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:52,050
His corrected theme keeps family context in view;
broader legal results are set aside.

10
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:59,150
One prepared fictional perspective appears.
No live community is connected.

11
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:05,250
Ravi says a trusted friend helped him speak with family.

12
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:12,200
Their circumstances differ: Arjun has not said
he has someone he trusts.

13
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:19,300
The exact question is for the Family Expectations group,
under the alias QuietRiver.

14
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:26,400
Private conversation is excluded.
Consent remains unchecked.

15
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:31,000
Arjun chooses Maybe later. Nothing is sent.

16
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,290
“I can ask for time before deciding.”
Kept privately for this preview.
